cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use repository-authored InclusiveShift-HAR software, cite this
  metadata and cite every third-party dataset separately under its own terms.
title: >-
  InclusiveShift-HAR: Auditable Wearable Activity Recognition under
  Population and Sensor-Interface Shift
type: software
version: 0.1.7a0
repository-code: https://github.com/abdullahuseyinli-dot/inclusive-shift-har
authors:
  - family-names: Huseyinli
    given-names: Abdulla
abstract: >-
  Evidence-gated research software for participant-exclusive inertial human
  activity recognition. The package contains the locked InclusiveHAR benchmark,
  participant-level evaluation, project-developed SpectralShape and GSP feature
  representations, RMRP denoising studies, CTGR/HERA selective posture pipelines,
  external sensor-interface diagnostics, and append-only records of corrections,
  negative outcomes and participant harms. InclusiveHAR trial boundaries remain
  unrecoverable. Later CTGR/HERA results are development evidence and do not
  establish clinical validity, state-of-the-art performance or independent
  superiority.
keywords:
  - human activity recognition
  - wearable sensing
  - inertial sensors
  - domain generalization
  - gravity-aware activity recognition
  - participant-exclusive evaluation
  - annotation leakage
  - reproducible research
license: Apache-2.0
